# VPS + Caddy: `handle_path /relay/*` strips the prefix, so this base URL ends in /relay.
# With no reverse proxy, use the server root and do not append /relay
# (http://127.0.0.1:18790 or http://100.x.y.z:18790). See docs/no-vps.md
# and docs/no-vps.zh-CN.md.
# Task attachments (--file) use chunked resumable PUT on v2 servers and multipart
# (RELAY_MAX_SOFT_BODY, default 16MiB) on old servers.
RELAY_URL=https://relay.example.com/relay
RELAY_SECRET_FILE=/path/to/relay/secret
RELAY_RESULTS_DIR=/workspace/relay-results
RELAY_WAKE_DIR=/workspace/relay/wake
# Optional backup relays, comma separated, tried in order after RELAY_URL.
# relay-box-agent consumes results from every channel at once; relay-send hands a
# task to the next channel if the Mac has not accepted it within RELAY_HANDOFF_S.
# See docs/channels.md. Example: box relay first, VPS (public, then tailnet) second.
# RELAY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:18790
RELAY_FALLBACK_URL=https://relay.example.com/relay,http://100.x.y.z:18791
# RELAY_HANDOFF_S=20
# How long relay-send waits for the worker to accept (state running, or already
# done/failed). On timeout the task stays queued: stderr prints 已入队、尚未接单
# and the process exits 2. Stdout is still the task id. Default 45. Enqueue
# failure is exit 1.
# RELAY_STARTED_WAIT_S=45
